		<chapter num="15">
			<heading>
				Joshua 15
			</heading>
			<heading>
				The Allotment for Judah
			</heading>
			<begin-paragraph>
			</begin-paragraph>
			<v n="1">the wilderness of Zin at the farthest south.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015002">
			</marker>
			<v n="2">Salt Sea, from the bay that faces southward.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015003">
			</marker>
			<v n="3">the ascent of Akrabbim, passes along to Zin, and goes up south of Kadesh-barnea, along by Hezron, up to Addar, turns about to Karka,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015004">
			</marker>
			<v n="4">the Brook of Egypt, and comes to its end at the sea. This shall be your south boundary.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015005">
			</marker>
			<v n="5">Salt Sea, to the mouth of the Jordan. And the boundary on the north side runs from the bay of the sea at the mouth of the Jordan.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015006">
			</marker>
			<v n="6">the stone of Bohan the son of Reuben.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015007">
			</marker>
			<v n="7">En-rogel.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015008">
			</marker>
			<v n="8">of Rephaim.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015009">
			</marker>
			<v n="9">that is, Kiriath-jearim).</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015010">
			</marker>
			<v n="10">Timnah.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015011">
			</marker>
			<v n="11">Baalah and goes out to Jabneel. Then the boundary comes to an end at the sea.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015012">
			</marker>
			<v n="12">the Great Sea with its coastline. This is the boundary around the people of Judah according to their clans.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015013">
			</marker>
			<v n="13">Hebron (Arba was the father of Anak).</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015014">
			</marker>
			<v n="14">Sheshai and Ahiman and Talmai, the descendants of Anak.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">Now the name of Debir formerly was Kiriath-sepher.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015016">
			</marker>
			<v n="16">And Caleb said, “He who attacks Kiriath-sepher and captures it, I will give him Achsah my daughter as wife.”</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015017">
			</marker>
			<v n="17">the brother of Caleb, captured it. And he gave him Achsah his daughter as wife.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015018">
			</marker>
			<v n="18">When she came to him, she urged him to ask her father for a field. And she dismounted from her donkey, and Caleb said to her, “What do you want?”</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015019">
			</marker>
			<v n="19">She said to him, “Give me a blessing. Since you have given me the land of the Negeb, give me also springs of water.” And he gave her the upper springs and the lower springs.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015020">
			</marker>
			<v n="20">This is the inheritance of the tribe of the people of Judah according to their clans.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015021">
			</marker>
			<v n="21">Eder, Jagur,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015022">
			</marker>
			<v n="22">Kinah, Dimonah, Adadah,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015023">
			</marker>
			<v n="23">Kedesh, Hazor, Ithnan,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015024">
			</marker>
			<v n="24">Ziph, Telem, Bealoth,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015025">
			</marker>
			<v n="25">Hazor-hadattah, Kerioth-hezron (that is, Hazor),</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015026">
			</marker>
			<v n="26">Amam, Shema, Moladah,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015027">
			</marker>
			<v n="27">Hazar-gaddah, Heshmon, Beth-pelet,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015028">
			</marker>
			<v n="28">Beersheba, Biziothiah,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015029">
			</marker>
			<v n="29">Baalah, Iim, Ezem,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015030">
			</marker>
			<v n="30">Eltolad, Chesil, Hormah,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015031">
			</marker>
			<v n="31">Ziklag, Madmannah, Sansannah,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015032">
			</marker>
			<v n="32">Lebaoth, Shilhim, Ain, and Rimmon: in all, twenty-nine cities with their villages.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015033">
			</marker>
			<v n="33">Eshtaol, Zorah, Ashnah,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015034">
			</marker>
			<v n="34">Zanoah, En-gannim, Tappuah, Enam,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015035">
			</marker>
			<v n="35">Azekah,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015036">
			</marker>
			<v n="36">Shaaraim, Adithaim, Gederah, Gederothaim: fourteen cities with their villages.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015037">
			</marker>
			<v n="37">Zenan, Hadashah, Migdal-gad,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015038">
			</marker>
			<v n="38">Dilean, Mizpeh, Joktheel,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015039">
			</marker>
			<v n="39">Eglon,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015040">
			</marker>
			<v n="40">Cabbon, Lahmam, Chitlish,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015041">
			</marker>
			<v n="41">Makkedah: sixteen cities with their villages.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015042">
			</marker>
			<v n="42">Libnah, Ether, Ashan,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015043">
			</marker>
			<v n="43">Iphtah, Ashnah, Nezib,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015044">
			</marker>
			<v n="44">Keilah, Achzib, and Mareshah: nine cities with their villages.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015045">
			</marker>
			<v n="45">Ekron, with its towns and its villages;</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015046">
			</marker>
			<v n="46">from Ekron to the sea, all that were by the side of Ashdod, with their villages.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015047">
			</marker>
			<v n="47">the Great Sea with its coastline.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015048">
			</marker>
			<v n="48">And in the hill country, Shamir, Jattir, Socoh,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015049">
			</marker>
			<v n="49">that is, Debir),</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015050">
			</marker>
			<v n="50">Anab, Eshtemoh, Anim,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015051">
			</marker>
			<v n="51">Giloh: eleven cities with their villages.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015052">
			</marker>
			<v n="52">Arab, Dumah, Eshan,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015053">
			</marker>
			<v n="53">Janim, Beth-tappuah, Aphekah,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015054">
			</marker>
			<v n="54">Hebron), and Zior: nine cities with their villages.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015055">
			</marker>
			<v n="55">Ziph, Juttah,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015056">
			</marker>
			<v n="56">Jezreel, Jokdeam, Zanoah,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015057">
			</marker>
			<v n="57">Timnah: ten cities with their villages.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015058">
			</marker>
			<v n="58">Halhul, Beth-zur, Gedor,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015059">
			</marker>
			<v n="59">Maarath, Beth-anoth, and Eltekon: six cities with their villages.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015060">
			</marker>
			<v n="60">Kiriath-baal (that is, Kiriath-jearim), and Rabbah: two cities with their villages.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015061">
			</marker>
			<v n="61">Beth-arabah, Middin, Secacah,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015062">
			</marker>
			<v n="62">Engedi: six cities with their villages.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015063">
			</marker>
			<v n="63">so the Jebusites dwell with the people of Judah at Jerusalem to this day.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v06015064">
			</marker>
			<end-paragraph>
			</end-paragraph>
		</chapter>
